course: dictionary
lesson: 10466
title: Tuck: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one is meant. Tuck is a good example. «She tucks her arm into Alice's and walks with her» means she pushes her arm in close to Alice's, like linking arms. It is not about food or bed.
explain: «Behind one drawn blind they see the shadow of a bird-cage and a little bird who wakes, yawns and tucks his head back in.» Here tuck means to pull something in close and out of the way. Ask yourself: what is being tucked, and where does it go?
explain: Tuck can also mean putting a child into bed with the covers snug around them. Look for clues like bed, blanket or covers. In swimming, a tuck is a body position with the knees pulled up to the chest, so the clue is the body and the sport.
fact: Tuck means to push a loose edge into a place so it stays neat, like a shirt tucked into trousers.
fact: Tuck in or tuck up can mean to put a child into bed with the covers pulled snugly around them.
fact: Tuck in can also mean to start eating food eagerly.
fact: «Tucked away» means hidden or in a safe place, out of the way.
fact: In old British school stories, a tuck shop or tuck means sweets and snacks.
exercise: «A tail tucked between the legs means the dog is scared.» What does tucked mean here? | Painted bright red | *Pushed in close and out of sight | Wagged happily | Cut right off
exercise: Mum says «Tuck in, everyone!» at dinner time. What does she mean? | Hide the food away | Sew a fold into the tablecloth | Go to bed early | *Start eating eagerly
exercise: «The bulge of Brazil tucks into the curve of West Africa.» What does tucks mean here? | *Fits snugly into a space | Shouts across | Cooks in a pan | Runs away from
test: In swimming, what is a tuck dive? | A dive with the head pointing down and the feet flat | A dive from a high board with no splash | *A dive with the knees pulled up to the chest | A dive with the arms stretched wide
test: Which phrase means hidden or out of the way? | tuck in | tuck shop | tuck jump | *tucked away
exam: Which meaning fits «Ella tucked the note into her pocket»? | Sewed a fold into cloth | Pulled a funny face | Ate a snack quickly | *Put something into a small, safe place
